        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/process/Process_CopyIntoFolio",
          "@type": "bootstrap:Process",
          "conformsTo": [
            "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/externalSchema/omg-bpmn-2.0",
            "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/externalSchema/omg-dd-1.0"
          ],
          "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/copy-into-folio.svg",
          "description": "Taking an asset from an upstream knowledge graph into your own folio so you can edit it, comment on it or raise todos against it — without touching the upstream source and without losing where it came from.\n\nThis is the fourth knowledge-graph affordance (`copy-into-folio` in `kg-affordances`). Like `copy-out-materialized.bpmn` for held library items, it is TWO WRITES AND A REFUSAL, gated up front by write capability:\n\n1. Check whether the session holds a write capability (`git-push`, `github-api`, or `github-connector`). When none is available, degrade cleanly to read-only inspection (`browse`) and emit the `KgAsset` declaration snippet with `source` pre-filled rather than failing mid-procedure.\n2. Read the asset and its origin (`instance`, `path`, `ref`) from the source knowledge graph without mutating the source.\n3. Copy the asset into the target folio, declare it in the folio's `assets[]`, and stamp `KgAsset.source` (`{ instance, path, ref }` — `AssetSourceSchema` in `schemas/kg/kg-node.ts`). `source` absent means authored locally (a third state), so omitting `source` on a copy is the defect this process exists to prevent.\n4. Verify the declared asset via `check:declaration-resolution` (`check:declared-assets`), then hand off to the folio author to edit, comment or raise todos on their copy.",
          "enforcement": "strict",
          "flowCount": 11,
          "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/directory/processes",
          "name": "Copy a knowledge-graph asset into a folio",
          "nodeCount": 12,
