        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/process/Process_GraphDetanglement",
          "@type": "bootstrap:Process",
          "conformsTo": [
            "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/externalSchema/omg-bpmn-2.0",
            "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/externalSchema/omg-dd-1.0"
          ],
          "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/graph-detanglement.svg",
          "description": "Part of a repository wants to leave, for size or a semantic reason: four gated stages measure it out of the graph before anything moves, and an administrator authorises the extraction. THE FOUR STAGES ARE GATES, NOT ADVICE: nothing moves until the stage before it measures zero, and they are drawn because a rule in prose is one an agent under pressure talks itself past. Each gate here is a DECISION TABLE: `workflow_complete` refuses a hand-supplied outcome at a `cat-harness.processes:decision` gateway, so the branch is computed from the counts a tool already produced rather than asserted.\n\nTHE SHARPEST GATE IS `Detangled?`, AND IT IS SHARP BECAUSE OF ITS RULE ORDER. `unassignedEdges &gt; 0` returns `unknown` BEFORE the cross-edge rule is reached, so a zero cross-edge count over an unjudged corpus cannot be read as a pass: unassigned edges are edges the tool declined to judge, not clean ones. A person can skip that rule; a table cannot.\n\nEVERY GATE HAS A THIRD STATE AND NONE OF THEM RENDERS IT AS CLEAN. `Declared in place?` answers `unknown` on a declaration that did not parse rather than \"not yet\", because one says the work has not started and the other says nobody can tell. `Detangled?` answers `unknown` on an incomplete measurement. Both route to `End_Unknown`, which is a REFUSAL to advance — the process stops rather than proceeding on a guess.\n\nDECLARING IS CHEAP AND EXTRACTING IS EXPENSIVE, WHICH IS THE POINT. Stage 1 moves nothing: the sub-graph is declared where it already sits, still inside the repository, still connected.\n\nSTAGE 2 IS A LOOP, AND THE LOOP IS LOAD-BEARING. `Prune, merge, factor, or reclassify` returns to `Measure` rather than to the gate, because an assignment is verified by RE-RUNNING and never by being locally reasonable. The four moves are the only four: the first three are the block-scale rule, and \"the classification is wrong\" is the fourth the repository scale adds because a module's layer is in doubt the way a block's chapter is not.\n\nISOLATION IS NOT ZERO EDGES. A sub-graph with no inbound edges can still carry no declaration, no namespace and no published artefact, and lifting that directory produces a repository that cannot say what it is. `bootstrap/` is the demonstrated case and the shape to match.\n\nTHE EXTRACTION IS A PERSON'S DECISION, AND THE LANE SAYS SO. `Authorise the extraction` sits in the Administrator lane because an extraction moves durable artefacts out of a repository, and `deletion-requires-confirmation` is not a courtesy the agent may waive: the agent reports what would move, and waits. The administrator lane is the one whose activities change the substrate every other diagram's lanes bind to, which is exactly what a repository cut does.",
          "enforcement": "strict",
          "flowCount": 18,
          "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/directory/processes",
          "name": "A sub-graph wants to leave",
          "nodeCount": 15,
          "sourcePath": "processes/kg/graph-detanglement.bpmn",
          "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness/blob/main/processes/kg/graph-detanglement.bpmn",
          "startNode": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/process/Process_GraphDetanglement/node/Start_Wants",
          "summary": "Part of a repository wants to leave, for size or a semantic reason: four gated stages measure it out of the graph before anything moves, and an administrator authorises the extraction."
        },
