          ],
          "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/session-state-machine.svg",
          "description": "The shape of a session from the outside: establish who is acting, open a record for them, take each turn in, and write down only what actually changed.\n\nYou are in this process for the whole of a session, underneath whatever else you are doing — it is the frame the other processes run inside. The first gateway is the one that matters: an agent that cannot say who is acting ASKS, because every later decision about permissions, preferences and language depends on an answer nobody guessed.\n\nThe distinction between refreshing a timestamp and writing what changed is the diagram's whole content. A session record that logs every turn as a change cannot be read for what happened, and one that logs none cannot be read at all.",
          "enforcement": "advisory",
          "flowCount": 14,
          "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/directory/processes",
          "name": "Session state machine",
          "nodeCount": 12,
          "sourcePath": "processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn",
          "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness/blob/main/processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn",
          "startNode": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/process/Process_SessionStateMachine/node/Start_Session",
          "summary": "The shape of a session from the outside: establish who is acting, open a record for them, take each turn in, and write down only what actually changed."
