          "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/archimate-publish.svg",
          "description": "An ArchiMate model is authored in Archi and committed; everything a reader sees is derived from it by three mechanical Tools, in order, in the pipeline lane: `archimate-check` (it parses and resolves), `archimate-metamodel` (the element types and relationship patterns it uses, each checked against ArchiMate's relationship table), and `archimate-pages` (a page and an IRI for every view, element and relationship, every view drawn, and the \"Metamodel in use\" page). No step draws a diagram by hand, and none runs Archi or a JVM (skill `archimate-models`).\n\nThe metamodel is the second step's output, so it cannot disagree with the model.",
          "enforcement": "strict",
          "flowCount": 7,
          "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/directory/processes",
