          ],
          "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/theme-ui-review.svg",
          "description": "Reviewing GRAPHICAL ASSETS AS THEY ARE INGESTED — accessibility, branding, languages — in the context of the website or app design they are for, to determine what the graphical assets and the UI are going to be.\n\nAT INGESTION ONLY: it is called from `ingest-theme.bpmn`.\n\nWHY THE MOMENT MATTERS. Reviewed after a build, a finding is a defect in something shipped. Reviewed at ingestion, the same finding is a decision about what the assets WILL be, taken while it is still cheap. The question the review asks is unchanged; the object it asks it of moved upstream, and so did the cost of the answer.\n\nThere is no role-to-theme mapping — theme choice remains an authoring judgement, per note — so nothing here checks a binding. What gets reviewed is the ingested art in its design context.",
          "enforcement": "advisory",
          "flowCount": 9,
          "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/directory/processes",
          "name": "Theme and UI review — at ingestion",
          "nodeCount": 9,
          "sourcePath": "processes/ui/theme-ui-review.bpmn",
